WEBVTT

00:09.680 --> 00:11.560
Now, Professor Otowa,

00:11.860 --> 00:15.870
if you want to pay off your debts,

00:15.870 --> 00:18.490
you will create your androids
to take over the world!

00:18.490 --> 00:21.870
Yes, my lord of evil!

00:36.140 --> 00:38.050
Go, my ClassicaLoids!

00:38.050 --> 00:39.940
Use your weird-ass powers to

00:39.940 --> 00:43.020
destroy the world or something!

00:47.810 --> 00:50.190
I don't get it anymore.

00:50.670 --> 00:52.900
What are the ClassicaLoids?

00:53.540 --> 00:55.320
Oh, haven't we told you?

00:55.560 --> 00:58.620
ClassicaLoids are us.

00:59.060 --> 01:01.510
ClassicaLoids?

01:01.810 --> 01:04.580
Yup. And they were created

01:05.670 --> 01:07.180
by me.

01:07.180 --> 01:08.630
Dad!

01:08.930 --> 01:11.100
Hey, I finally got a connection.

01:11.100 --> 01:11.970
Kyougo.

01:11.970 --> 01:13.710
Hey, it's Kyo-kun.

01:13.930 --> 01:17.330
Hey, Beethes, Motes, you made it.

01:17.330 --> 01:18.640
Good, good.

01:19.180 --> 01:21.250
Is that Otowa Kyougo?

01:21.250 --> 01:22.850
And who are you?

01:22.850 --> 01:23.860
I'm Liszt.

01:24.180 --> 01:25.270
This here is Cho-chan.

01:25.550 --> 01:28.320
Ah, so you awoke, too.

01:28.320 --> 01:29.860
That's brilliant.

01:29.040 --> 01:30.110
Where are you?!

01:30.110 --> 01:31.300
When are you coming back?

01:31.300 --> 01:33.110
What were you doing this whole time?

01:33.110 --> 01:34.360
What is a ClassicaLoid?

01:35.680 --> 01:39.160
Your temper gets more
and more like your mother.

01:39.160 --> 01:39.850
What?!

01:39.850 --> 01:42.910
ClassicaLoids are my creation.

01:42.910 --> 01:43.620
Huh?

01:43.620 --> 01:44.910
Wait, they're your illegitimate kids?!

01:45.170 --> 01:46.280
They are.

01:46.280 --> 01:48.630
I never told you, Kanae,

01:48.630 --> 01:50.540
but you have eight older
brothers and sisters.

01:50.540 --> 01:51.530
What?!

01:51.530 --> 01:52.820
Just kidding.

01:53.610 --> 01:55.280
Don't "a ha ha" me!

01:55.280 --> 01:56.510
You made them?

01:56.800 --> 01:57.920
They're robots?!

01:57.920 --> 01:59.010
No way.

01:59.360 --> 02:01.930
Their bodies are the same
as any other person's.

02:01.930 --> 02:05.310
I just kind of put them
together, and it worked.

02:05.310 --> 02:07.270
Oh, really?

02:07.630 --> 02:09.440
But what for?

02:09.440 --> 02:12.020
I got captured by an evil organization.

02:12.550 --> 02:16.210
They threatened me into creating
superhumans for world domination.

02:16.510 --> 02:17.700
Nah, I'm just messing.

02:19.150 --> 02:21.210
Just get back here.

02:21.210 --> 02:24.790
Do you have any idea how much trouble this
place has seen because of your debts?

02:24.790 --> 02:26.340
See, that's why

02:26.340 --> 02:28.880
I sent Beethes and Motes over.

02:28.880 --> 02:31.230
They've got some amusing talents, right?

02:31.230 --> 02:32.120
Have they not done it yet?

02:32.120 --> 02:34.130
You're talking about Musik, right?

02:34.370 --> 02:35.240
That's it.

02:35.240 --> 02:39.050
I figured they might be able to make
use of that to put a dent in the debt.

02:39.520 --> 02:41.180
Dent in the debt?

02:41.670 --> 02:43.860
Is that why we're here?

02:44.400 --> 02:46.900
You're the who ran up those debts, Dad.

02:46.900 --> 02:49.740
Get back here and find some work—

02:48.620 --> 02:51.080
Uh-oh, my signal's getting weak.

02:51.080 --> 02:52.650
I might get cut off.

02:51.950 --> 02:52.650
Hey!

02:52.900 --> 02:55.400
Just take care of them for me.

02:55.700 --> 02:58.190
It'll be fine, you're a strong girl.

02:58.190 --> 02:59.500
Dad!

02:59.500 --> 03:00.400
I'll call you later.

03:04.530 --> 03:05.530
Huh?!

03:05.530 --> 03:07.460
What was I...

03:09.270 --> 03:10.670
Made them?

03:11.000 --> 03:12.530
This is all so sudden.

03:14.870 --> 03:17.220
It's not like I'm strong
because I want to be.

03:18.110 --> 03:18.910
Idiot.

04:50.890 --> 04:54.440
06: "The Beginning of the ClassicaLoids"

04:52.770 --> 04:54.440
Morning, Kanae!

04:54.440 --> 04:56.050
Good morning.

05:01.650 --> 05:03.750
Want some, girl?

05:03.750 --> 05:04.940
See you.

05:08.110 --> 05:10.030
Lud-kun, Kanae's being weird.

05:10.330 --> 05:12.790
She didn't tell me to stop
messing up the hallway floor.

05:13.200 --> 05:14.200
Indeed.

05:14.490 --> 05:18.290
Normally, she would have seen this and
fired a barrage of complaints at me.

05:18.670 --> 05:22.670
My day doesn't begin until Kanae scolds me.

05:23.090 --> 05:24.920
Maybe she's done with you two.

05:25.220 --> 05:28.770
You're here to help with
the debts, aren't you?

05:28.770 --> 05:31.310
Have you ever made any money?

05:31.310 --> 05:32.060
Nope.

05:32.360 --> 05:34.200
Well, there you go.

05:34.470 --> 05:36.340
She probably decided to
kick you out officially,

05:36.340 --> 05:38.520
since there's no point
having you guys around.

05:38.520 --> 05:39.830
Wha?

05:39.830 --> 05:42.650
She doesn't need to think about money.

05:42.650 --> 05:44.790
But my little kitten does.

05:45.820 --> 05:49.060
I need only to make money, correct?

05:54.660 --> 05:55.880
What's wrong?

05:55.880 --> 05:58.430
Things are so complicated.

05:58.430 --> 06:01.040
I don't know how to approach them.

06:01.380 --> 06:02.290
With who?

06:02.290 --> 06:03.650
The freeloaders.

06:03.650 --> 06:05.500
Oh, Motes-san and the others?

06:05.860 --> 06:07.420
Can't you just keep things
the way they were?

06:07.790 --> 06:10.010
I thought they were just a bunch of people

06:10.010 --> 06:12.130
with a serious lack of common sense.

06:12.410 --> 06:15.330
I don't even know if they're people anymore.

06:34.140 --> 06:35.780
"Hello, world."

06:35.780 --> 06:37.160
Hello, world.

06:37.160 --> 06:38.900
Nice to meet you.

06:39.290 --> 06:40.460
You understand what I'm saying, right?

06:40.950 --> 06:42.420
How do you feel?

06:50.310 --> 06:53.750
Bach-sama, Tchaiko-kun and
Bąda-kun have arrived.

06:55.080 --> 06:56.770
I apologize.

06:57.790 --> 07:01.270
I tried to take them back
using Musik, but...

07:01.940 --> 07:04.190
I accept all responsibility.

07:04.700 --> 07:06.610
Poco a poco.

07:08.530 --> 07:09.800
Adagio.

07:10.400 --> 07:12.660
Understood.

07:14.530 --> 07:15.450
Tchaiko-kun,

07:15.890 --> 07:18.580
what did Bach-sama say earlier?

07:19.050 --> 07:20.610
Same thing as before.

07:20.610 --> 07:22.700
"Leave them be."

07:23.000 --> 07:24.080
I see.

07:24.770 --> 07:27.190
He seems to have some kind of plan.

07:27.490 --> 07:31.380
Well, it looks like you
should stay put for now.

07:34.080 --> 07:35.740
I hate her.

07:35.740 --> 07:37.610
She's so snotty.

07:38.190 --> 07:40.020
"Some kind of plan..."

07:40.020 --> 07:41.780
If only I could know what it was.

07:45.310 --> 07:49.110
A child's responsible for
what her parents make, huh?

07:49.580 --> 07:52.080
It's not like they commit
crimes or anything.

07:52.380 --> 07:55.360
I should just keep acting
like their landlord, right?

07:56.130 --> 07:58.630
I'll just make sure they pay rent.

07:59.350 --> 08:00.110
Yeah.

08:01.000 --> 08:06.500
Smiley Gyoza-kan

08:06.500 --> 08:10.010
Smiley Gyoza-kan?

08:10.400 --> 08:10.960
You!

08:11.280 --> 08:12.820
That table goes over there.

08:12.820 --> 08:14.300
Move it quickly.

08:14.520 --> 08:17.350
Quickly?
This thing's heavy as hell.

08:17.680 --> 08:19.550
Quit complaining.

08:20.670 --> 08:22.330
Ah, girl, you're home.

08:22.330 --> 08:24.120
You're late, Kanae.

08:24.120 --> 08:25.630
Help us out.

08:25.630 --> 08:27.460
What are you doing?

08:27.460 --> 08:28.500
What?

08:28.500 --> 08:30.350
I thought we were opening
a gyoza specialty shop.

08:30.350 --> 08:31.070
What?!

08:31.330 --> 08:33.750
Lud-kun, are we putting this away, too?

08:33.750 --> 08:34.710
Leave this here.

08:35.210 --> 08:38.240
I'll be upgrading it into a gyoza machine.

08:39.820 --> 08:42.160
Hey, look, isn't it adorable?

08:42.440 --> 08:43.500
Hasshie!

08:43.830 --> 08:46.320
Hey, we have a mascot for the shop?

08:46.320 --> 08:47.750
It's not cute.

08:47.750 --> 08:50.630
Let's put boobs on it!

08:51.260 --> 08:52.260
Begin.

08:55.680 --> 09:00.180
G-Get out, all of you!

09:07.850 --> 09:12.140
Tomorrow's the day that
I finally kick them all out.

09:14.980 --> 09:15.920
Huh?

09:19.200 --> 09:21.950
Gyoza is Firepower

09:19.200 --> 09:21.950
Gyoza

09:28.240 --> 09:29.180
They're gone.

09:45.700 --> 09:48.860
How do you feel being awake, Beethes?

09:48.860 --> 09:49.810
Beethes?

09:50.180 --> 09:51.650
My name is Ludwig van...

09:51.650 --> 09:53.450
Just call yourself Beethes.

09:53.990 --> 09:55.780
And you're Motes.

09:55.780 --> 09:56.530
Motes?

09:57.350 --> 10:01.160
I hate to get straight to business,
but I need you two to come with me.

10:01.520 --> 10:02.390
Why?

10:02.390 --> 10:04.210
Why? Well...

10:04.210 --> 10:06.010
Let's see...

10:06.620 --> 10:10.070
Because it'll be more fun that way, I guess.

10:15.310 --> 10:18.190
Looks like you both like gyoza.

10:18.740 --> 10:20.920
I don't like that

10:20.920 --> 10:22.330
"Motes" and "Beethes" business.

10:22.330 --> 10:23.510
It sounds cheap.

10:23.760 --> 10:25.060
Relax.

10:25.060 --> 10:27.130
You have to start somewhere.

10:27.130 --> 10:29.660
When in Rome, do as the Romans do.

10:29.660 --> 10:30.940
Don't be so stuck up.

10:31.340 --> 10:32.770
We aren't...

10:33.070 --> 10:35.130
You're Beethes and Motes.

10:35.850 --> 10:37.440
It's my decision.

10:37.740 --> 10:39.080
So it's settled.

10:41.060 --> 10:43.030
"Go here."

10:41.990 --> 10:46.160
Go here

10:43.030 --> 10:46.160
"My daughter's here. Make friends with her."

10:47.020 --> 10:48.100
Where's Kyo-kun?

10:48.400 --> 10:49.160
He's gone.

10:50.570 --> 10:52.040
Wait a second,

10:52.830 --> 10:54.230
did we just get abandoned?

10:57.580 --> 10:58.760
Are we here?

10:59.020 --> 11:00.690
This looks fun.

11:01.970 --> 11:02.890
Um...

11:03.170 --> 11:06.140
Are you two looking to move in?

11:29.300 --> 11:30.490
Bach?

11:30.490 --> 11:32.000
What are you talking about?

11:32.360 --> 11:35.840
This is <i>the</i> Johann Sebastian Bach.

11:36.260 --> 11:39.560
I'm telling you that he's the
reincarnation of the great Bach-sama.

11:39.860 --> 11:41.340
So, what,

11:41.600 --> 11:45.690
this AlcheLoid wouldn't
awaken no matter what,

11:45.690 --> 11:48.470
until you made it listen to Bach's music,

11:48.470 --> 11:51.100
and now it's awakened,
and it thinks it's Bach?

11:51.640 --> 11:53.950
Not "it," he's the great Bach-sama.

11:54.530 --> 11:55.880
ClassicaLoid.

11:56.770 --> 11:57.960
ClassicaLoid!

11:57.960 --> 11:59.320
That's a brilliant name.

11:59.610 --> 12:01.610
Who gave you that right?

12:02.270 --> 12:05.130
You're Professor Otowa's
assistant, are you not?

12:05.130 --> 12:07.030
Just what is the professor doing?

12:07.030 --> 12:10.000
The professor is tuning
the other ClassicaLoids.

12:10.000 --> 12:13.030
I was moved by the great Bach-sama.

12:13.030 --> 12:15.460
I've decided to follow him
for the rest of my life.

12:15.930 --> 12:19.460
You'd understand if you heard
his performance, executives.

12:19.810 --> 12:21.660
Performance, you say?

12:23.620 --> 12:25.530
Cantabile!

12:31.240 --> 12:32.760
Bravo!

12:32.760 --> 12:34.170
Lord of music!

12:34.170 --> 12:35.980
Father of music!

12:36.340 --> 12:39.070
Brilliant, great Bach-sama!

12:39.070 --> 12:42.660
The great Bach-sama is
opening a recital today

12:42.660 --> 12:45.840
in acknowledgment of the executives.

12:45.840 --> 12:48.200
I expect you to work even harder.

12:48.200 --> 12:49.440
Yes, ma'am!

12:54.600 --> 12:56.150
Are you ready?

12:56.710 --> 12:57.690
Understood.

12:57.690 --> 12:58.710
I'll be right there.

13:02.210 --> 13:04.450
It looks like she's up to something.

13:06.280 --> 13:07.420
You're right.

13:07.720 --> 13:09.490
I think they're legit gone.

13:09.960 --> 13:11.100
I'm going to get changed.

13:12.400 --> 13:13.780
Put the tables back.

13:13.780 --> 13:15.520
What? Why me?

13:16.300 --> 13:17.690
What do you expect?

13:17.690 --> 13:19.330
No one else is here anymore.

13:19.330 --> 13:20.330
But...

13:21.380 --> 13:22.190
They're back!

13:23.170 --> 13:24.590
Welcome...

13:26.250 --> 13:28.200
Here're your papers.

13:28.700 --> 13:32.140
We're going to resume the demolition
project that got interrupted.

13:32.140 --> 13:32.910
Huh?

13:33.230 --> 13:36.190
I thought the demolition was called off.

13:36.190 --> 13:37.820
Circumstances changed.

13:37.820 --> 13:40.590
We <i>really</i> need to level this place.

13:40.590 --> 13:42.130
We can't back down.

13:43.400 --> 13:45.980
I'm not selling this house.
Please leave.

13:45.980 --> 13:47.480
It's too late for that!

13:47.480 --> 13:48.840
The contract's been signed!

13:49.340 --> 13:53.050
I promised myself that I'd protect this house...

13:53.050 --> 13:54.370
My grandmother's house!

13:54.370 --> 13:56.090
Don't be absurd!

13:56.090 --> 13:57.090
Open the door!

13:57.090 --> 13:57.730
I will not!

13:58.010 --> 13:59.700
This is bad.

13:58.460 --> 14:00.870
Hey! That's enough!

13:59.700 --> 14:01.260
Sousuke, barricade!

14:00.870 --> 14:02.360
Open up!

14:01.260 --> 14:02.000
Okay.

14:03.870 --> 14:07.860
Well, if you insist you're Bach,
then I guess you're Bach.

14:08.190 --> 14:11.060
You've showed up in this world after

14:11.060 --> 14:13.370
260 or 270 years or so.

14:14.000 --> 14:16.790
People haven't really changed much, have we?

14:17.380 --> 14:19.720
If you have unfinished business,

14:19.720 --> 14:21.640
why don't you give it a try?

14:25.600 --> 14:28.340
This is definitely the right town.

14:28.960 --> 14:31.610
I definitely saw Beethoven-senpai here.

14:33.840 --> 14:34.820
This way?

14:35.780 --> 14:36.490
No...

14:37.290 --> 14:38.140
Here!

14:38.140 --> 14:39.240
Come on!

14:39.240 --> 14:40.070
Get out!

14:40.070 --> 14:40.800
Damn it!

14:40.800 --> 14:41.820
Open up!

14:43.770 --> 14:46.650
Open up, or we're ripping it open.

14:46.920 --> 14:48.360
Are you listening?

14:49.270 --> 14:50.360
Open!

14:51.330 --> 14:53.370
Are you okay with this?

14:53.750 --> 14:55.820
I haven't seen anything.

14:55.820 --> 14:57.200
I don't know anything.

14:57.590 --> 14:58.950
Go away!

14:58.950 --> 15:01.380
This is my precious home.

15:01.610 --> 15:03.690
I told you, that won't cut it.

15:03.690 --> 15:05.250
Let's break in.

15:05.250 --> 15:06.510
Ready, and...

15:09.840 --> 15:11.550
All right, charge!

15:13.000 --> 15:14.570
Isn't this taking it too far?

15:14.870 --> 15:17.350
Let's calm down for a second, guys.

15:30.200 --> 15:31.640
Stop it!

15:32.950 --> 15:34.630
Please, just not that.

15:34.630 --> 15:36.260
All right, miss, out of the way.

15:36.260 --> 15:37.510
Let me go.

15:37.510 --> 15:39.860
You're going to get crushed
if you stay here.

15:39.860 --> 15:41.670
No. Let go!

15:41.670 --> 15:43.580
Stop!

15:45.010 --> 15:46.210
The girl.

15:47.230 --> 15:48.210
Kanae.

15:48.910 --> 15:50.050
My little kitten.

15:54.110 --> 15:55.540
Damn it, let go!

15:55.540 --> 15:56.820
Let go!

15:56.820 --> 15:59.020
All right, begin.

16:00.560 --> 16:02.380
Stop!

16:03.110 --> 16:06.480
Somebody help!

16:07.360 --> 16:10.740
Spielen wir unsere

16:11.020 --> 16:13.490
Musik!

16:16.430 --> 16:18.490
N-Not that robot again!

16:18.740 --> 16:22.120
Fate, destroy me if you can!

16:22.490 --> 16:23.620
Beethes-san.

16:33.360 --> 16:34.190
There it is.

16:37.770 --> 16:40.430
I'm not dreaming. I'm not
dreaming. I'm not dreaming.

16:40.430 --> 16:41.940
I've finally found you.

16:41.940 --> 16:43.020
I've found you for real this time,

16:43.390 --> 16:46.980
Beethoven-senpai!

16:50.820 --> 16:52.850
Isn't that Shuu-san?

16:52.850 --> 16:53.890
What...

16:57.050 --> 16:59.710
You're actually pretty cute.

16:59.710 --> 17:00.800
So are you.

17:01.500 --> 17:02.990
Would you dance with me?

17:02.990 --> 17:04.120
Gladly.

17:06.420 --> 17:07.630
Liszt-san.

17:10.050 --> 17:11.840
Wh-What's going on?

17:14.810 --> 17:17.180
Eek, strangers!

17:17.610 --> 17:18.890
Chopin-san.

17:22.270 --> 17:24.080
I wanna join in!

17:24.080 --> 17:24.640
Motes-san.

17:28.220 --> 17:29.320
Go!

17:33.100 --> 17:34.750
Wh-What's going on?

17:35.200 --> 17:37.640
The Musik is mixing together.

18:12.830 --> 18:14.650
My head's going to explode.

18:15.080 --> 18:16.010
What is...

18:16.650 --> 18:18.320
My body...

18:18.760 --> 18:20.240
...is moving by itself.

18:20.600 --> 18:22.160
I can't stop.

18:22.620 --> 18:23.760
Huh?

18:24.380 --> 18:26.830
Tchaiko-chan, do something.

18:28.530 --> 18:30.330
What's going on?

19:09.150 --> 19:10.620
It's back.

19:10.620 --> 19:11.880
What was that?

19:12.580 --> 19:14.280
"Toccata and Fugue."

19:14.280 --> 19:18.230
A famous organ piece composed
by Johann Sebastian Bach.

19:18.550 --> 19:21.880
I-It's a real haunted house.

19:22.760 --> 19:24.050
Hey, wait up.

19:26.860 --> 19:29.460
Is this Musik?

19:29.460 --> 19:30.680
But whose?

19:30.980 --> 19:32.350
It's <i>that</i> man.

19:32.700 --> 19:33.860
What man?

19:34.230 --> 19:36.490
Haven't you met him?

19:37.140 --> 19:40.490
The father of music, Johann Sebastian Bach.

19:41.630 --> 19:44.620
It looks like he helped us
for some reason, though.

19:45.850 --> 19:46.940
Bach.

19:58.910 --> 19:59.840
Kanae.

20:03.990 --> 20:04.970
We're home.

20:05.560 --> 20:07.340
Are you safe, girl?

20:18.140 --> 20:19.670
Why are you crying?

20:20.560 --> 20:21.860
It's all right.

20:21.860 --> 20:23.740
Cry, my little kitten.

20:31.800 --> 20:32.870
I'm sorry.

20:33.610 --> 20:37.130
I got ahead of myself, trying to
make up for Tchaiko-kun's error.

20:37.760 --> 20:40.010
I still hate her.

20:45.850 --> 20:48.010
So, who are you?

20:48.960 --> 20:51.310
Beethoven-senpai, it's me!

20:51.310 --> 20:52.850
Four-eyes, right?

20:53.170 --> 20:54.450
No!

20:54.450 --> 20:56.300
My name is Schubert!

20:56.300 --> 20:57.830
And who the hell are you?

20:57.830 --> 20:59.590
Mozart. You can call me Motes.

20:59.590 --> 21:00.890
Mozart?!

21:00.890 --> 21:02.490
So you were behind this!

21:04.480 --> 21:07.490
I need to talk to all of you.

21:09.820 --> 21:12.890
You can stay at Otowakan if you wish.

21:12.890 --> 21:16.380
But you'll follow the rules strictly.

21:16.680 --> 21:19.210
Beethes-san, no cooking outside the kitchen.

21:19.470 --> 21:22.380
Motes-san, no riding down the
hallway on your roller shoes.

21:22.680 --> 21:24.960
Chopin-san, no making a nest in your room.

21:24.960 --> 21:28.390
Liszt-san, please stop hugging me and stuff.

21:28.690 --> 21:29.400
And me?

21:29.400 --> 21:31.390
You don't even live here, Sousuke!

21:31.730 --> 21:35.190
Lastly, Beethes-san, Motes-san,
you two will be paying rent.

21:35.470 --> 21:37.890
You're getting no respect
from me until you pay rent.

21:37.890 --> 21:39.610
I'm calling you Beethes and Motes.

21:42.810 --> 21:43.990
Do as you wish.

21:43.990 --> 21:46.880
Woot! It's like a special relationship.

21:46.880 --> 21:49.370
Oh yeah, so where were you guys?

21:49.650 --> 21:53.500
My little kitten was so angry
yesterday, remember?

21:53.500 --> 21:55.710
We went to find her

21:55.710 --> 21:58.080
presents to help her feel better.

21:59.640 --> 22:01.920
I received this in exchange
for helping some fishers.

22:01.920 --> 22:02.840
Enjoy it.

22:04.450 --> 22:07.430
I got this for you from
some friendly misters.

22:06.300 --> 22:07.430
Yummy Shredded Squid

22:07.980 --> 22:09.590
These are new on the market.

22:09.590 --> 22:12.010
Go get some hot guys
with your all-out pheromones.

22:12.280 --> 22:13.970
You can have this rare item.

22:14.480 --> 22:15.550
I don't need it.

22:15.550 --> 22:17.430
You don't need to thank us.

22:17.430 --> 22:19.930
This is a profitable
alternative to paying rent.

22:19.930 --> 22:21.320
I never said that.

22:21.320 --> 22:24.240
Hey, let's have a "The House Is Safe" party!

22:24.240 --> 22:25.720
I'll go get drinks.

22:25.720 --> 22:27.610
I'll make gyoza.

22:28.670 --> 22:30.620
I just told you...

22:32.270 --> 22:34.850
Enough!

22:34.850 --> 22:37.730
Hey! Beethes! Motes!

22:37.730 --> 22:39.500
You're getting no respect from me!

22:39.500 --> 22:40.920
Stop! Motes!

22:40.000 --> 22:43.000
To be continued

22:40.920 --> 22:43.000
Stop right there!

24:12.970 --> 24:27.440
07: "Mountain King"

24:13.540 --> 24:16.800
Unidentified Mysterious Animals.

24:16.800 --> 24:19.730
Also known as UMAs.

24:19.730 --> 24:21.560
Are they a sign of the apocalypse?

24:21.560 --> 24:23.580
All must prepare.

24:23.580 --> 24:26.230
Face the moon, and cry, "Mommy!"

24:26.230 --> 24:28.600
It's the legendary Hamagon.
